The said section is reproduced hereinunder:-
"26A. Inspection - (1) A State Council may, with the previous sanction of the State Government, appoint Inspectors having the prescribed qualifications for the purpose of Chapters III, IV and V of this Act.
(2) An Inspector may- (a) inspect any premises where drugs are compounded or dispenses and submit a written report to the Registrar;
(b) enquire whether a person who is engaged in compounding or dispensing of drugs is a registered pharmacist;
